From a3daff0700f2c6e88cd75596ca2f638858df2bfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 00:20:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] selftests/dax: add the CRAM tier tests

Add selftests exercising the CRAM compressed-RAM tier on a CPU-less
N_MEMORY_PRIVATE node, driven from a dax/kmem device via its [TEST] sysfs
and the cram debugfs control:

   - node lifecycle and registration, ops, ratio and balloon, trim,
     pressure, perf.
   - the anonymous tier: demote, read-in-place, COW-on-write promotion,
     swap-out, fork, hot-page promotion, and leak/gate checks.
   - the resident clean-file tier (cram_pgcache): mmap read in place,
     byte-write promotes off, drop_caches evicts.  Large/PMD folios
     (cram_pgcache_large).  Readahead and sequential read served in
     place, splice promotes (cram_readahead).
   - adversarial coherence (cram_coherence): generation-stamped hashing
     hunts for stale or torn reads and for writes leaking through to the
     read-only tier.

run_all.sh drives the suite under virtme-ng and drops caches between
tests.

Signed-off-by: Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-8
